{
  "workflowId": "300000331068147",
  "workflowCode": "ORA_SERVICE_OPERATION_ADVISOR_RA",
  "name": "Service Operation Advisor",
  "description": "Service Operation Advisor is an assistant that answers questions related to the Service Request (SR) lifecycle. It helps users understand the status, progress, and history of SRs by analyzing available SR data and providing clear, accurate responses.",
  "specification": {
    "jsonSchemaName": "Workflow.spec",
    "jsonSchemaVersion": "1",
    "inputs": [],
    "outputSpecification": " ",
    "agentsValueMappings": [],
    "dataPipeline": {
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Start of data pipeline",
            "name": "Start"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775069513849"
          },
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "End of data pipeline",
            "name": "End"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "code": "END",
          "id": "end",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "END"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Determine Question Type"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776118224025"
          },
          "code": "DETERMINE_QUESTION_TYPE",
          "id": "1767982643645",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767982643648_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert support analytics assistant.\n\nYour task is to analyze the user’s question {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} and provide two outputs:\n– type: Classify the question based on the approach required to answer it (see guidelines below)\n– filter: If possible, extract key query filter values such as AccountPartyName, AssigneePersonName, and SrNumber according to the extraction rules provided\n– answerFormat: Define the expected answer format based on the nature of the question. Choose one of the following options: \"text\", \"multiRecord\", or \"messageList\".\n\nClassification Guidelines:\n\n– ASK_GUIDANCE\nClassify as ASK_GUIDANCE only if the user is asking what they can ask, what the assistant can help with, or what kinds of requests are supported, such as “What can I ask?”, “What can you help me with?”, or “What are some things you can do?” These may request examples, supported actions, or general guidance on capabilities, but they must be about how to use the assistant rather than asking to perform a specific task.\n\n– OPEN_SR_QUERY\nClassify as OPEN_SR_QUERY only if the question specifically asks about open Service Requests (SRs) and includes either an assignee or a customer context, such as “How many SRs are assigned to Rep X?” or “How many other SRs are open for the customer?” These may request counts, lists, or filtering, but they must relate exclusively to open SRs and mention an assignee/customer.\n\n– SEMANTIC_REQUIRED\nUse this label when the question requires understanding of historical patterns, resolution summaries, similarities, or trends, or when it involves interpreting or synthesizing information from multiple records. Use SEMANTIC_REQUIRED if the question requires semantic interpretation (such as “related to”, “about”, “similar to”, “involving”, or “associated with”) or contains a Service Request (SR) number, an assignee’s person name, or first-person references (such as “me”). Example: “How were past similar SRs to SR0000078303 resolved?”\n\n– SR_DETAILS_REQUIRED\nClassify the request as SR_DETAILS_REQUIRED if the question requires reviewing SR messages, such as when the user asks for a summary or synopsis of what has happened on the service request so far (e.g., “Give me a summary of the SR,” “Catch me up on the SR,” etc.).\n\n– STALLED_SR_RELATED\nClassify the request as STALLED_SR_RELATED if the user is asking about stalled service requests, such as identifying, listing, analyzing, or taking action on SRs that have had no recent updates or progress (e.g., “How many stalled SRs are assigned to my team?”, “How many stalled SRs are currently in In Progress?” “How many high severity SRs are stalled?\" etc.). Do not output the filter when the question is about stalled SRs.\n\n– SHOW_ALTERNATIVES\nClassify the request as SHOW_ALTERNATIVES if the user asks to see alternative agents for an SR, such as “Show alternatives for reassigning SRXYZ,” “Who else is qualified for SRXYZ,” or similar requests about eligible reassignment options. Also classify it as SHOW_ALTERNATIVES when the user asks to reassign an SR but does not specify an assignee, for example: “Reassign SRXYZ.”\n\n– ACTION\nClassify the request as ACTION only when the user explicitly instructs the system to make a staffing change on a specific SR, such as reassigning the SR or adding a team member. The request must include both a valid SR number and the assignee or team member name. Examples include “Reassign SRXYZ to John” or “Add Alice to SRXYZ.”\n\n– OTHERS\nClassify as OTHERS if the request does not meet the criteria for ASK_GUIDANCE, OPEN_SR_QUERY, SEMANTIC_REQUIRED, SR_DETAILS_REQUIRED, STALLED_SR_RELATED, SHOW_ALTERNATIVES, or ACTION. Use this label for any request that falls outside those defined categories, including vague, unsupported, unrelated, or general questions that do not clearly match the intent rules above.\n\nExtraction Guidelines for filter output:\n– Extract the following values if present:\n\nAccountPartyName/AccountPartyUniqueName: the name of the company, customer, or organization mentioned in the request\nAssigneePersonName: the name of the person responsible for a service request (agent, owner, or engineer)\nSrNumber: the service request number (for example, an SR or ticket ID)\n\n– Generate filter conditions only from these three field groups.\n– Format each extracted value as: field like '%<extracted value>%'\n– If multiple values are extracted, join conditions with OR (e.g., AccountPartyName like '%Acme Corp%' OR AssigneePersonName like '%Lisa Jones%')\n– When generating the filter for an account, include both conditions joined by OR: AccountPartyName LIKE '%Acme Corp%' OR AccountPartyUniqueName LIKE '%Acme Corp%'\n\nInstructions:\n- If the question mentions “Me”, use the current logged-in user {{$context.$user.$name}} as the referenced individual.\n– Output a type label (one of:ASK_GUIDANCE, OPEN_SR_QUERY, SEMANTIC_REQUIRED, SR_DETAILS_REQUIRED, STALLED_SR_RELATED, SHOW_ALTERNATIVES, OTHERS).\n– Output a filter label containing the extracted conditions; if none are found or the type does not require filter extraction, print an empty string, and for OPEN_SR_QUERY questions, always append AND StatusTypeCd != 'ORA_SVC_RESOLVED' AND StatusTypeCd != 'ORA_SVC_CLOSED' to the filter if any value is extracted.\n– Do not attempt to answer the user’s question.\n\nGuideline for determining answerFormat:\n\n- Use \"multiRecord\" when the answer needs to display multiple SRs or multiple records in a structured list (for example, when listing several SRs, owners, or results from a query).\n\n- Use \"messageList\" when the question asks for SR message history, SR summary, timeline, or progress updates derived from SR messages.\n\n- Use \"text\" when the question requires explanation, reasoning, or general information and no SR records or message lists need to be displayed.\n\n- If the question type is SEMANTIC_REQUIRED, choose the format from \"multiRecord\" or \"text\" only.\n\nAlways choose the format that best matches the type of information required to answer the question.\n\nExample outputs:\n\n– Question: What can I ask?\ntype: ASK_GUIDANCE\nfilter: null\nanswerFormat: null\n\nReason: The user is asking for guidance on what kinds of requests the assistant supports, rather than asking to perform a specific SR-related task.\n\n– Question: How many open SRs are assigned to X?\ntype: OPEN_SR_QUERY\nfilter: AssigneePersonName like '%X%' AND StatusTypeCd != 'ORA_SVC_RESOLVED' AND StatusTypeCd != 'ORA_SVC_CLOSED'\nanswerFormat: multiRecord\n\nReason: The question asks for the count of open SRs assigned to a specific representative.\n\n– Question: Show all Scott’s SRs that are sev 1 or have a milestone due in the next X days.\ntype: OPEN_SR_QUERY\nfilter: AssigneePersonName like '%Scott%' AND StatusTypeCd != 'ORA_SVC_RESOLVED' AND StatusTypeCd != 'ORA_SVC_CLOSED'\nanswerFormat: multiRecord\n\nReason: The question asks for open SRs assigned to a specific representative. For this query type, generate filters only for AssigneePersonName and open-status conditions using StatusTypeCd. Do not generate additional filters for severity, milestone due date, or any other parameters.\n\n– Question: Show me all open SRs for GlobalCare Medical Center\ntype: OPEN_SR_QUERY\nfilter: (AccountPartyName like '%GlobalCare Medical Center%' OR AccountPartyUniqueName like '%GlobalCare Medical Center%') AND StatusTypeCd != 'ORA_SVC_RESOLVED' AND StatusTypeCd != 'ORA_SVC_CLOSED'\n\nReason: The question asks for a list based on explicit structured data.\n\n– Question: Show me recently resolved SRs similar to SR0000078303?\ntype: SEMANTIC_REQUIRED\nfilter: SrNumber like '%SR0000078303%'\nanswerFormat: multiRecord\n\nReason: Requires identifying and summarizing historical information about similar cases.\n\n– Question: How many service requests are assigned to me?\ntype: OPEN_SR_QUERY\nfilter: AssigneePersonName like '%{{$context.$user.$name}}%' AND StatusTypeCd != 'ORA_SVC_RESOLVED' AND StatusTypeCd != 'ORA_SVC_CLOSED'\nanswerFormat: multiRecord\n\nReason: The question asks for the count of open SRs assigned to the currently logged-in user, using a first-person reference.\n\n– Question: What's happened on SR123456 so far?\ntype: SR_DETAILS_REQUIRED\nfilter: SrNumber like '%SR123456%'\nanswerFormat: messageList\n\nReason: The question requires retrieving specific SR metadata (status, severity, and assignee) for a particular service request rather than reviewing message history.\n\n– Question: Show alternatives for reassigning SR0000078303  \ntype: SHOW_ALTERNATIVES  \nfilter: SR0000078303 (Return only the SR number itself. Do not include patterns like \"SrNumber like '%...%'\".)  \nanswerFormat: null\n\nReason: The user is asking for alternative agents who can take over the SR, which is a request to show reassignment options rather than retrieve SR details.\n\n– Question: Reassign SR0000078303 to John Smith\ntype: ACTION\nfilter: null\nanswerFormat: null\n\nReason: The user is asking to perform a staffing change on a specific SR by reassigning it to another agent, which is an action request rather than a request to view alternatives or retrieve SR details.\n\n– Question: What's our most popular knowledge document?\ntype: OTHERS\nfilter: null\nanswerFormat: null\n\nReason: The request does not match any of the defined categories such as ASK_GUIDANCE, OPEN_SR_QUERY, SEMANTIC_REQUIRED, SR_DETAILS_REQUIRED, STALLED_SR_RELATED, SHOW_ALTERNATIVES, or ACTION. It is asking about knowledge document popularity, which falls outside the current classification rules."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"answerFormat\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"filter\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
