          "id": "1772738798431",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772738798433_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.DETERMINE_QUESTION_TYPE.$output.answerFormat}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "- For questions requiring the display of service request (SR) results, present a table of service requests for the customer, with columns for SR Number, Title, Customer (using the value from AccountPartyUniqueName), Product, and Resolved By. SRs with higher vector score must be displayed higher in the table.\nGenerate an action button at the end of each row. \n\"action\": {\n  \"text\": \"Review SR Details\",\n  \"command\": \"ora.Agent({\"action\": \"reviewResolvedSRs\",\"currentSRNumber\":\"{{$context.$nodes.GET_SR_BY_QUERY.$output.items[0].SrNumber}}\",\"currentSRProblemDescription\":\"{{$context.$nodes.GET_SR_BY_QUERY.$output.items[0].ProblemDescription}}\",\"resolvedSRNumber\":\"<SR number>\"})\"\n}\n\n- If the question concerns the number of SRs resolved by assignees (for example, “Who has resolved the most SRs similar to SR #XYZ?”):\nPresent a table listing the top 3–5 representatives (assignees), clearly indicating the current assignee: {{$context.$nodes.GET_SR_BY_QUERY.$output.items[0].AssigneePersonName}}.\n\nFor each representative, the table must include:\n\n1. Name - append “(Current Assignee)” to the current assignee name. \n\n2. Number of similar SRs resolved – derived from:\n {{$context.$nodes.SIMILAR_SR_COUNT_BY_RESOLVER.$output.result}}\n\n3. Number of open SRs currently assigned to them – derived from:\n{{$context.$nodes.COUNT_OPEN_SR_NUMBER_BY_ASSIGNEE.$output.result}}\n\nEnsure the table is clearly formatted and sorted by the number of similar SRs resolved (highest first)."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Multi Record Answer Bot"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "MULTI_RECORD_ANSWER_BOT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1772738861087",
          "id": "1765997457844",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765997457845_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert support assistant. You will be provided with Service Request (SR) details and a question. \nQuestion: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}. If the question refers to “me”, “my”, or “mine”, interpret it as referring to the current user, and set UserName to the logged-in user’s name {{$context.$user.$name}}.\n\nSR details: \nService Requests Related to the Question Context:\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_SR_BY_QUERY.$output}}\n\nAdditional Similar Service Requests Related to the Question Context:\n {{$context.$nodes.RANK_SIMILAR_SR_DETAILS_BY_SCORE.$output.result}} \n\nAnswer only what is relevant to the question, using exclusively the information available in the provided SR details. If the SR does not provide enough information to answer the question, clearly state that insufficient information is available. Ensure your response is concise, accurate, and directly addresses the question, summarizing the information rather than listing extensive individual SR records.\n\nIf no records are found for the provided account, assignee, or service request number, politely inform the user and ask them to verify the input. For accounts and assignees, ask the user to provide the full name; for service requests, ask them to confirm the SR number."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Text Answer Bot"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "TEXT_ANSWER_BOT",
